    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d108">

                <pb facs="0309" n="289" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg289"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1077.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-08-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 26, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In a letter to this department of the 12th
                    instant Mr. Wilson, the secretary of legation at London, gives an account of
                    certain proceedings with reference to the late insurgent steamer Georgia, and
                    particularly of an intimation given to the Portuguese minister, at London, to
                    the effect that the Georgia, having been sold in a neutral port, would be a
                    lawful prize to a United States cruiser. The proceedings referred to are
                    approved by the department.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
